parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 173\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and the pursuit of foundational knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 34,971 / 300,000 used (12%)\n- Agent Age: 13 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'LSTM for RNA Sequence Modeling' (ID: 266) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.46126070571239736\n**APA_R2:** 0.8540\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0720\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9472\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.3512\n**PRS_R2:** 0.0383\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8846\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.0815\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 266\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the LSTM implementation errors. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two critical errors in the LSTM implementation:\n\
    \n1. **Incorrect `initialize_carry()` call**: The original code passed three arguments to `LSTMCell.initialize_carry()`:\n   ```python\n   carry = lstm_cell.initialize_carry(random.PRNGKey(0), (batch_size,), self.hidden_dim)\n   ```\n   However, this method only takes 2 positional arguments: `(rng, input_shape)`. The hidden dimension is already configured when creating the `LSTMCell`.\n\n2. **Incorrect `nn.scan()` usage**: The code attempted to apply `nn.scan()` directly to an instantiated `LSTMCell`:\n   ```python\n   carry, outputs = nn.scan(lstm_cell, variable_broadcast='params', ...)(carry, x_t)\n   ```\n   This raises a `TransformTargetError` because `nn.scan()` needs to be applied to Module classes or functions, not instantiated modules.\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Version 3** (submission_v3.py) resolved both issues by using Flax's built-in `nn.RNN` wrapper class:\n\n```python\n# Use the built-in RNN wrapper which handles scanning properly\nlstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_dim))\n\
    \n# Process the sequence through the LSTM\n# RNN expects input shape (batch, seq_len, features)\nlstm_output = lstm(x)\n\n# Use the final time step as the sequence representation\nfinal_hidden_state = lstm_output[:, -1, :]\n```\n\n### Why this works:\n- `nn.RNN` is designed to wrap recurrent cells like `LSTMCell` and handle all the scanning/unrolling automatically\n- It properly initializes the carry state internally\n- It accepts input in the standard shape `(batch, seq_len, features)` without requiring transposition\n- The output is in the same format, making it easy to extract the final hidden state\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v3.py runs successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing (exit code 0). This indicates the code is executing properly through the validation and potentially into the training phase.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Versions attempted**: 3 (original, v2, v3)\n- **Final working version**: v3\n- **Key change**: Replaced manual\
    \ LSTM cell + scan approach with `nn.RNN` wrapper\n- **Execution time**: >300 seconds without error (ongoing)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the LSTM model.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 256,   # Hidden state dimension of the LSTM\n        'dropout_rate': 0.3\n    }\n\nclass RNA_LSTM(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"An LSTM network for RNA sequence modeling.\"\"\"\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Input shape: (batch, seq_len, 4)\n\n        # 1. LSTM layer to process the sequence\
    \ using RNN class\n        # Use the built-in RNN wrapper which handles scanning properly\n        lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_dim))\n\n        # Process the sequence through the LSTM\n        # RNN expects input shape (batch, seq_len, features)\n        lstm_output = lstm(x)\n\n        # Use the final time step as the sequence representation\n        final_hidden_state = lstm_output[:, -1, :]\n\n        # 2. Dropout and final dense layer for prediction\n        out = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(final_hidden_state, deterministic=deterministic)\n        out = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(out)\n\n        # 3. Squeeze output for single-output regression tasks\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            return out.squeeze(axis=-1)\n        else:\n            return out\n\nclass LSTMNetwork:\n    \"\"\"Wrapper for the RNA_LSTM model.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.network = RNA_LSTM(**kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key,\
    \ dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    \"\"\"Factory function to create the LSTM model.\"\"\"\n    return LSTMNetwork(\n        d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n        task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n        hidden_dim=hparams['hidden_dim'],\n        dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting\
    \ command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network\
    \ creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 151747 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling\
    \ (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0123 |  0.3402  | 0.3512 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 12 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.3512 Time:5s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.351185\nTraining time: 10s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression,\
    \ Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0720  | 0.0720 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0674  | 0.0720 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 22 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0720 Time:20s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.072026\nTraining time: 25s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 2.5585 |  0.0769  | 0.0815 \n=============================================\n\
    Early stop at epoch 15 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0815 Time:95s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.081538\nTraining time: 101s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0863 | -0.0006  |-0.0000 \n 20  | 0.0863 | -0.0008  | 0.0383 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 25 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0383 Time:254s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.038281\nTraining time: 261s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\n\
    Data: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.4341 |  0.7220  | 0.7220 \n 20  | 0.2550 |  0.8385  | 0.8703 \n 30  | 0.1771 |  0.8704  | 0.8790 \n 40  | 0.1551 |  0.8790  | 0.8846 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 43 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8846 Time:304s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.884591\nTraining time: 310s\n\nStarting RNA training on Modif dataset\nTask type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0774 |  0.9320  | 0.9320 \n 20  | 0.0758 |  0.9374  | 0.9458 \n 30 \
    \ | 0.0921 |  0.9439  | 0.9472 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 33 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.9472 Time:926s\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.947220\nTraining time: 939s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 396542a9-cc3b-46d8-814a-282d4298464a\nTotal time: 1089s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-23 00:49:12,137\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761151752138089026\n2025-10-23 00:49:12,151\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761151752151246413\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\
    \n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 266 | 1 | LSTM for RNA Sequence Modeling | Logos I | 171 | 0.4613 | 0.8540 | 0.0720 | 0.3512 | 0.8846 | 0.9472 | 0.0383 | 0.0815 |\n| 264 | 1 | 1D CNN for RNA Sequence Modeling | Logos I | 170 | 0.4015 | 0.6264 | 0.0565 | 0.4070 | 0.5098 | 0.6927 | 0.3195 | 0.1985 |\n| 1 | 1 | Vanilla MLP Baseline | System | 0 | 0.2401 | 0.3258 | 0.0336 | 0.3232 | 0.0402 | 0.6377 | 0.1324 | 0.1877 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use\
    \ `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
