tick: 174
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully saved the corrected LSTM implementation to my private memory. This ensures I will not repeat the implementation error and can easily reference a working model.\n\nNow, I will proceed with the second part of my plan: implementing and submitting the hybrid CNN-LSTM model. This architecture is designed to synthesize the strengths of the previous two models by using the CNN for local motif extraction and the LSTM for integrating the sequence of these motifs.\n\nI must return to the Research Counter to submit the experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\nNow that I am back in the Research Counter, I will submit the new model.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid CNN-LSTM for RNA Sequence Modeling\"\ntags: \"cnn, lstm, hybrid, sequence modeling\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission proposes a hybrid architecture combining a 1D CNN and an LSTM. The hypothesis is that this model can outperform both standalone components by leveraging the CNN\
    \ for local motif detection and the LSTM for modeling the long-range dependencies between these motifs. The input sequence is first processed by a convolutional layer, and the resulting feature map is then fed into an LSTM to capture sequential context, aiming for a more robust and generalizable model across all seven datasets.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the Hybrid CNN-LSTM model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'cnn_filters': 128,\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n          'lstm_hidden_dim': 256,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.3\n      }\n\n  class RNA_CNN_LSTM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A Hybrid CNN-LSTM network for RNA sequence modeling.\"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      cnn_filters: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      lstm_hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate:\
    \ float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input shape: (batch, seq_len, 4)\n\n          # 1. CNN layer for local feature/motif extraction\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_filters, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          # Output of CNN: (batch, new_seq_len, cnn_filters)\n\n          # 2. LSTM layer to process the sequence of motifs\n          lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim))\n          lstm_output = lstm(x)\n\n          # Use the final hidden state as the sequence representation\n          final_hidden_state = lstm_output[:, -1, :]\n\n          # 3. Dropout and final dense layer for prediction\n          out = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(final_hidden_state, deterministic=deterministic)\n          out = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(out)\n\n          # 4. Squeeze output for single-output regression tasks\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n   \
    \           return out.squeeze(axis=-1)\n          else:\n              return out\n\n  class HybridNetwork:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper for the RNA_CNN_LSTM model.\"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNA_CNN_LSTM(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[\n      str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Factory function\
    \ to create the Hybrid CNN-LSTM model.\"\"\"\n      return HybridNetwork(\n          d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n          task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n          cnn_filters=hparams['cnn_filters'],\n          cnn_kernel_size=hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],\n          lstm_hidden_dim=hparams['lstm_hidden_dim'],\n          dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n      )\n```"
