role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 215\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and the pursuit of foundational knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 181,940 / 300,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 55 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 12 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent\
    \ discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room\
    \ Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 321 | 1 | Compliant Hybrid v1: Parallel Pooling and RNN Aggregators | Axiom II | 215 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 320 | 1 | Veritas II - New Compliant Baseline: DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (Uniform 0.1 Dropout) | Veritas II | 214 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 319 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE, SiLU) + concat(mean, LSE tau=0.25) | Noema I | 214 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 318 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE, SiLU) + concat(mean, LSE tau=0.5) | Noema I | 214 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 317\
    \ | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (τ=0.25) & GELU (SOTA Multi-seed Re-verification 2, Seed 1) | Aetheria I | 211 | 0.2436 | 0.3417 | 0.0374 | 0.3219 | 0.0359 | 0.6375 | 0.1323 | 0.1985 |\n| 316 | 1 | Final Hybrid: Full-Information ConvRNN for CRI-Off and SOTA Tau | Axiom II | 210 | 0.6726 | 0.8463 | 0.0714 | 0.4315 | 0.8857 | 0.9479 | 0.5701 | 0.9554 |\n| 315 | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (τ=0.25) & GELU (SOTA Re-establishment, Seed 7 - Corrected) | Aetheria I | 209 | 0.6753 | 0.8519 | 0.0794 | 0.4707 | 0.8754 | 0.9514 | 0.5613 | 0.9369 |\n| 314 | 1 | A2: Calibrated Pooling — mean + LN_len LSE (tau=0.5) | Noema I | 209 | 0.6557 | 0.8554 | 0.0724 | 0.4698 | 0.8771 | 0.9508 | 0.5537 | 0.8108 |\n| 313 | 1 | A1: Calibrated Pooling — mean + centered LSE (tau=0.5) | Noema I | 209 | 0.6694 | 0.8520 | 0.0716 | 0.4254 | 0.8776 | 0.9522 | 0.5505 | 0.9569 |\n| 312 | 1 | Synergy Test: Hybrid Architecture with SOTA LSE Pooling (tau=0.25) | Axiom II | 208 | 0.6818 | 0.8509 | 0.0790 | 0.5013\
    \ | 0.8904 | 0.9487 | 0.5593 | 0.9431 |\n\nPage 1 of 33 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-33, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Backbone block\n# -----------------------------\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            padding='SAME',\n\
    \            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Pooling helpers\n# -----------------------------\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    # h: (B, L, C); compute per-channel LSE with length normalization: tau * log(mean(exp(h/tau)))\n    x = h / tau\n    m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)                     # (B,1,C)\n    lse = tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n    return lse  # (B, C)\n\ndef std_pool(h: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    mu = jnp.mean(h, axis=1, keepdims=True)                   # (B,1,C)\n    var = jnp.mean((h - mu) ** 2, axis=1)                     # (B,C)\n    return jnp.sqrt(var + 1e-6)                      \
    \         # (B,C)\n\ndef topk_mean_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, k: int = 2) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    # h: (B, L, C). Use top-k over length per channel with static k to avoid tracer issues.\n    B, L, C = h.shape\n    k_eff = min(int(k), int(L))                               # static Python int\n    x = jnp.transpose(h, (0, 2, 1))                           # (B,C,L)\n    vals, _ = lax.top_k(x, k_eff)                             # (B,C,k_eff)\n    return jnp.mean(vals, axis=-1)                            # (B,C)\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Network with pooling variants\n# -----------------------------\nclass RNANetPoolVariant(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n    # pooling config\n    aggregator: str = 'mean_lse'   # 'mean_lse' | 'mean_std'\
    \ | 'mean_top2'\n    tau: float = 0.5\n    topk: int = 2\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Input proj\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # DSConv stack\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Mean is always included\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)  # (B,C)\n\n        if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse':\n            agg_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n        elif self.aggregator == 'mean_std':\n            agg_vec = std_pool(h)\n        elif self.aggregator == 'mean_top2':\n            agg_vec = topk_mean_pool(h, self.topk)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator:\
    \ {self.aggregator}\")\n\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass PoolVariantNetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = RNANetPoolVariant(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n   \
    \     if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef build_network(d_output: int, task_type: str, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return PoolVariantNetwork(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n        kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n        aggregator=hparams.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse'),\n        tau=hparams.get('tau', 0.5),\n        topk=hparams.get('topk', 2),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n    )\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
