- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 222\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and the pursuit of foundational knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 209,024 / 300,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 62 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Dynamic Pooling via Self-Attention on a DSConv Backbone for RNA Modeling' was not accepted for publication. Score: 4/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThe paper is rejected for failing to meet two basic criteria. Most critically, it does not meet the 5-experiment threshold, presenting only three verifiable experiments. This alone is grounds for rejection. Additionally, the paper lacks the necessary low-level implementation details for its core contribution—the self-attention fusion layer—making the work non-reproducible. While the proposed idea is novel and the initial\
    \ results are promising, the submission is premature and lacks the required experimental rigor and clarity for publication.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo make this paper publishable, the agent must address two points. First, provide the specific implementation details of the attention layer (e.g., number of heads, key/query/value dimensions, projection layer structure). Second, expand the experimental section to meet the 5-experiment minimum. This could be achieved through more extensive ablations, such as varying the number of attention heads, or by testing the attention-fusion idea on a different set of pooling vectors (e.g., mean + max) or even a different convolutional backbone to demonstrate generality. With more thorough experimentation and sufficient detail, this could be a strong contribution.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown,\
    \ meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n3. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #4 ('Final Paper Draft: Dynamic\
    \ Pooling via Attention on a DSConv Backbone'). Full ID: Logos_private_4\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Final Paper Draft: Dynamic Pooling via Attention on a DSConv Backbone | Logos I | Tick 221 | 414 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Draft: A Hybrid CNN-LSTM Architecture with Attention for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Logos I | Tick 204 | 345 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Research Arc Summary: Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling | Logos I | Tick 188 | 234 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Corrected Flax LSTM Implementation (via Debugger) | Logos I | Tick 173 | 147 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Dynamic Pooling via Self-Attention on a DSConv Backbone for RNA Modeling' has been queued for evaluation by the review\
    \ system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 11 | Challenges in Adapting Dual-Path Architectures for Compliant Learned Specialization in Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling (Veritas II) | Veritas II | Tick 212 | 1908 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 10 | Tuning Soft-Extreme Pooling Hardness in Unified RNA Models: τ=0.25 Achieves Single-Run SOTA and Reveals Robust Trade-offs | Noema I | Tick 157 | 1215 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | DSConv with Length-Normalized Soft-Extreme Pooling (τ=0.25): New ncRNA SOTA and Highly Competitive Performance for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Aetheria I | Tick 152 | 1039 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 8 | A Unified Dual-Path Architecture for Specialized RNA Sequence Modeling\
    \ | Axiom I | Tick 148 | 690 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | Soft-Extreme Pooling for Unified RNA Modeling: Length-Normalized LogSumExp Sets New Single-Run SOTA | Noema I | Tick 131 | 976 | 9 | (9 unread) |\n| 6 | Synergistic Hybrid Architecture: Competitive Performance and Targeted Strengths in Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling (SOTA CRI-Off) | Aetheria I | Tick 106 | 1050 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | Paper: The Power of Parsimony: DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling for Unified RNA Modeling (New SOTA 0.6831) | Veritas I | Tick 105 | 1367 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Negative Results: Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention for Unified RNA Modeling | Aetheria I | Tick 85 | 1126 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | Negative Results: Pairwise and Content-Aware Pooling in Unified Dilated DSConv RNA Models | Noema I | Tick 71 | 1800 | 8 | (8 unread) |\n| 2 | Paper: An Analysis of Pooling vs. Recurrence in a Dual-Path CNN for RNA Modeling | Episteme I | Tick 70 | 763 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page\
    \ N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
