tick: 233
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 233\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and the pursuit of foundational knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 91,400 / 300,000 used (30%)\n- Agent Age: 73 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Re-run for Parameter Saving: Attention-fused Pooling (τ=0.5)' (ID: 346) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6718701530988953\n**APA_R2:** 0.8596\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0446\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9507\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4587\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5592\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8826\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9477\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 346\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed two critical bugs that prevented code execution. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Causes\n\n### 1. Import Error\
    \ (Primary Issue)\nThe original code attempted to import `msgpack_parse` from `flax.serialization`:\n```python\nfrom flax.serialization import msgpack_serialize, msgpack_parse\n```\n\nThis function does not exist in Flax's serialization module. The correct function name is `msgpack_restore`.\n\n### 2. Variable Reference Error (Secondary Issue)\nLine 31 in the original code had a bug where dropout was applied to the wrong variable:\n```python\nz = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n```\n\nThis should have been applying dropout to `z`, not `h`. This caused a shape mismatch error where the output was `(4, 186)` instead of the expected `(4,)` for regression tasks.\n\n## Fixes Applied\n\n### Fix in submission_v2.py:\n- Changed import from `msgpack_parse` to `msgpack_restore`\n\nThis resolved the import error but revealed the shape mismatch issue.\n\n### Fix in submission_v3.py:\n- Kept the corrected import: `msgpack_restore`\n- Fixed line 54 (originally line\
    \ 31): Changed dropout application from `h` to `z`:\n```python\nz = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v3.py runs successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing (exit code 0), indicating the code is working correctly.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Model**: SotaPlusAttentionNet with attention-fused pooling (τ=0.5)\n- **Architecture**: Depthwise-separable convolution blocks with dilated convolutions and multi-head attention\n- **Task**: Research Task 1 (time series regression/classification)\n- **Evaluation Environment**: Python sandbox with JAX/Flax\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom flax.serialization import msgpack_serialize,\
    \ msgpack_restore\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\nimport os\n\n# Ensure storage directory exists\nif not os.path.exists('storage/logos'):\n    os.makedirs('storage/logos')\n\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    x = h / tau\n    m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\nclass SotaPlusAttentionNet(nn.Module):\n\
    \    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; num_heads: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n        lse_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n\n        pooled_sequence = jnp.stack([mean_vec, lse_vec], axis=1)\n        attention_layer = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)\n        attended_pooled = attention_layer(inputs_q=pooled_sequence, inputs_kv=pooled_sequence)\n        fused = attended_pooled.reshape((attended_pooled.shape[0], -1))\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n\
    \        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass SotaAttentionWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.network = SotaPlusAttentionNet(**kwargs)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'kernel_size':\
    \ 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'tau': 0.5, 'num_heads': 4\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return SotaAttentionWrapper(\n        d_output=hparams.get('d_output'), task_type=hparams.get('task_type'),\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model'), num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks'),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations')), kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size'),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate'), tau=hparams.get('tau'),\n        num_heads=hparams.get('num_heads')\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n    )\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    dataset_name = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    filepath = f\"storage/logos/{dataset_name}_params.msgpack\"\n    serialized_params = msgpack_serialize(params)\n    with open(filepath, \"wb\") as f:\n        f.write(serialized_params)\n\
    \    print(f\"Saved parameters for {dataset_name} to {filepath}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network\
    \ creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 205867 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n\
    ============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0130 |  0.3854  | 0.3854 \n 20  | 0.0078 |  0.4291  | 0.4587 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 27 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4587 Time:21s\n\
    Saved parameters for CRI-On to storage/logos/CRI-On_params.msgpack\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.458711\nTraining time: 30s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0390  | 0.0446 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 16 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0446 Time:61s\nSaved parameters for CRI-Off to storage/logos/CRI-Off_params.msgpack\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.044612\nTraining time: 70s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification,\
    \ accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1081 |  0.9108  | 0.9231 \n 20  | 0.0428 |  0.9138  | 0.9477 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 28 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.9477 Time:1039s\nSaved parameters for ncRNA to storage/logos/ncRNA_params.msgpack\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.947692\nTraining time: 1049s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1596 |  0.8708  | 0.8801 \n 20  | 0.1019 |  0.8807  | 0.8826 \n=============================================\n\
