tick: 235
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 235\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and the pursuit of foundational knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 100,752 / 300,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 75 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Analysis of Attention Weights' (ID: 349) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** n.a.\n**APA_R2:** None\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** None\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** None\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** None\n**PRS_R2:** None\n**MRL_R2:** None\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** None\n**Evaluation Details:** Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 349\n\n## Summary\n✅ **SUCCESS** - Fixed the code to run without crashing. The submission now successfully analyzes attention weights across all 7 datasets.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code attempted to use `return_attention=True`\
    \ parameter with Flax's `MultiHeadDotProductAttention`, but this parameter doesn't exist in the Flax API. The error was:\n\n```\nTypeError: MultiHeadDotProductAttention.__call__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'return_attention'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the attention weight extraction mechanism to use Flax's proper intermediate collection system:\n\n### Changes in `submission_v2.py`:\n\n1. **Removed invalid parameter**: Deleted `return_attention=True` from the attention layer call\n\n2. **Added proper weight collection**: Used `sow_weights=True` parameter instead:\n   ```python\n   attended_pooled = attention_layer(inputs_q=pooled_sequence, inputs_kv=pooled_sequence,\n                                     deterministic=deterministic, sow_weights=True)\n   ```\n\n3. **Modified model return signature**: Changed from returning `(logits, attn_weights)` to just `logits`, since attention weights are now stored in intermediates\n\n4. **Updated model.apply() call**: Added `mutable=['intermediates']`\
    \ to capture sowed weights:\n   ```python\n   _, intermediates = model.apply({'params': params}, dummy_input, deterministic=True,\n                                  mutable=['intermediates'])\n   ```\n\n5. **Extracted weights from intermediates**: Retrieved attention weights from the intermediates collection:\n   ```python\n   attn_weights = intermediates['intermediates']['MultiHeadDotProductAttention_0']['attention_weights'][0]\n   ```\n\n## Results\nThe fixed code successfully:\n- Analyzed all 7 RNA datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA)\n- Extracted and displayed attention weight patterns for each dataset\n- Revealed interesting patterns (e.g., MRL dataset shows 100% attention to 'mean', CRI-On shows 74% attention to 'lse')\n- Completed without any errors\n\nThe task is now functioning as intended, providing insights into how the attention mechanism weights the mean vs. LSE pooling representations across different RNA prediction tasks.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The\
    \ debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom flax.serialization import msgpack_serialize, msgpack_restore\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\nimport os\n\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float)\
    \ -> jnp.ndarray:\n    x = h / tau\n    m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\nclass SotaPlusAttentionNet(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; num_heads: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n        lse_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n\n        pooled_sequence = jnp.stack([mean_vec, lse_vec], axis=1)\n\n        # We need to capture the attention weights using sow_weights=True\n\
    \        attention_layer = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)\n        attended_pooled = attention_layer(inputs_q=pooled_sequence, inputs_kv=pooled_sequence,\n                                          deterministic=deterministic, sow_weights=True)\n\n        fused = attended_pooled.reshape((attended_pooled.shape[0], -1))\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        # Return only logits; attention weights are in intermediates\n        return logits\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'tau': 0.5, 'num_heads': 4\n    }\n\ndef test():\n    print(\"--- Starting Attention Weight Analysis ---\")\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n\
    \    key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n\n    dataset_configs = {\n        \"APA\": {\"max_seq_len\": 186, \"d_output\": 1},\n        \"CRI-Off\": {\"max_seq_len\": 46, \"d_output\": 1},\n        \"Modif\": {\"max_seq_len\": 101, \"d_output\": 12},\n        \"CRI-On\": {\"max_seq_len\": 23, \"d_output\": 1},\n        \"PRS\": {\"max_seq_len\": 148, \"d_output\": 3},\n        \"MRL\": {\"max_seq_len\": 100, \"d_output\": 1},\n        \"ncRNA\": {\"max_seq_len\": 1136, \"d_output\": 13},\n    }\n\n    for ds_name, config in dataset_configs.items():\n        print(f\"\\n--- Analyzing Dataset: {ds_name} ---\")\n        filepath = f\"storage/logos/{ds_name}_params.msgpack\"\n\n        if not os.path.exists(filepath):\n            print(f\"ERROR: Parameter file not found at {filepath}\")\n            continue\n\n        with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:\n            serialized_params = f.read()\n\n        params = msgpack_restore(serialized_params)\n\n        model = SotaPlusAttentionNet(\n        \
    \    d_output=config[\"d_output\"], task_type=\"regression\", # task_type doesn't affect this part\n            d_model=hparams['d_model'], num_blocks=hparams['num_blocks'],\n            dilations=tuple(hparams['dilations']), kernel_size=hparams['kernel_size'],\n            dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'], tau=hparams['tau'],\n            num_heads=hparams['num_heads']\n        )\n\n        dummy_input = jnp.ones((1, config[\"max_seq_len\"], 4))\n\n        # Use mutable=['intermediates'] to capture attention weights\n        _, intermediates = model.apply({'params': params}, dummy_input, deterministic=True,\n                                       mutable=['intermediates'])\n\n        # Extract attention weights from intermediates\n        attn_weights = intermediates['intermediates']['MultiHeadDotProductAttention_0']['attention_weights'][0]\n\n        # attn_weights shape is (batch, num_heads, q_len, kv_len) -> (1, 4, 2, 2)\n        # We want to see the weights on the two input\
    \ vectors (mean, lse)\n        # Let's average across the heads\n        avg_attn_weights = jnp.mean(attn_weights, axis=1).squeeze()\n\n        print(f\"Average Attention Weights (across heads):\")\n        print(f\"  - Query 'mean' attends to 'mean': {avg_attn_weights[0, 0]:.4f}\")\n        print(f\"  - Query 'mean' attends to 'lse':  {avg_attn_weights[0, 1]:.4f}\")\n        print(f\"  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'mean': {avg_attn_weights[1, 0]:.4f}\")\n        print(f\"  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'lse':  {avg_attn_weights[1, 1]:.4f}\")\n\n    return \"Analysis Complete.\"\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\n--- Starting Attention Weight Analysis ---\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: APA ---\nAverage Attention Weights (across heads):\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'mean': 0.7500\n  - Query 'mean'\
    \ attends to 'lse':  0.2500\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'mean': 0.7500\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'lse':  0.2500\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: CRI-Off ---\nAverage Attention Weights (across heads):\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'mean': 0.5003\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'lse':  0.4997\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'mean': 0.5002\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'lse':  0.4998\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: Modif ---\nAverage Attention Weights (across heads):\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'mean': 0.5000\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'lse':  0.5000\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'mean': 0.5000\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'lse':  0.5000\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: CRI-On ---\nAverage Attention Weights (across heads):\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'mean': 0.2569\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'lse':  0.7431\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'mean': 0.2537\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'lse':  0.7463\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: PRS ---\nAverage Attention Weights (across heads):\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'mean':\
    \ 0.5000\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'lse':  0.5000\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'mean': 0.5000\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'lse':  0.5000\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: MRL ---\nAverage Attention Weights (across heads):\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'mean': 1.0000\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'lse':  0.0000\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'mean': 1.0000\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'lse':  0.0000\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: ncRNA ---\nAverage Attention Weights (across heads):\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'mean': 0.2500\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'lse':  0.7500\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'mean': 0.2500\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'lse':  0.7500\nTest completed. Result: Analysis Complete.\n=== Test Mode Complete ===\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research\
    \ Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 349 | 1 | Analysis of Attention Weights | Logos I | 233 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 348 | 1 | Replication: Axiom II Gumbel-Gated MoE (exact code), seed=7 | Noema I | 233 | 0.6720 | 0.8487 | 0.0745 | 0.4850 | 0.8883 | 0.9500 | 0.5654 | 0.8923 |\n| 347 | 1 | Replication: Axiom II Gumbel-Gated MoE (exact code), seed=42 | Noema I | 233 | 0.6681 | 0.8495 | 0.0770 | 0.4654 | 0.8936 | 0.9488 | 0.5596 | 0.8831 |\n| 346 | 1 | Re-run for Parameter Saving: Attention-fused Pooling (τ=0.5) | Logos I | 231\
